{
  "id": "29c713ce-bbcf-48c8-a0fe-59b40a37bbb4",
  "page_title": "'How to use global batch processing with Azure OpenAI Service'",
  "page_description": "Learn how to use global batch with Azure OpenAI Service",
  "page_date": "08/12/2024",
  "chunk_title": "Global batch support",
  "chunk_content": "Global batch support  ### Region and model support  Global batch is currently supported in the following regions:  - East US - West US - Sweden Central  The following models support global batch:  | Model | Version | Supported | |---|---|---| |`gpt-4o` | 2024-05-13 |Yes (text + vision) | |`gpt-4o-mini` | 2024-07-18  | Yes (text + vision) | |`gpt-4` | turbo-2024-04-09 | Yes (text only) | |`gpt-4` | 0613 | Yes | | `gpt-35-turbo` | 0125 | Yes | | `gpt-35-turbo` | 1106 | Yes | | `gpt-35-turbo` | 0613 | Yes |   Refer to the models page for the most up-to-date information on regions/models where global batch is currently supported.  ### API Versions  - `2024-07-01-preview`  ### Not supported  The following aren't currently supported:  - Integration with the Assistants API. - Integration with Azure OpenAI On Your Data feature.  ### Global batch deployment  In the Studio UI the deployment type will appear as `Global-Batch`.  :::image type=\"content\" source=\"../media/how-to/global-batch/global-batch.png\" alt-text=\"Screenshot that shows the model deployment dialog in Azure OpenAI Studio with Global-Batch deployment type highlighted.\" lightbox=\"../media/how-to/global-batch/global-batch.png\":::  > [!TIP] > Each line of your input file for batch processing has a `model` attribute that requires a global batch deployment name. For a given input file, all names must be the same deployment name. This is different from OpenAI where the concept of model deployments does not exist.  ::: zone pivot=\"programming-language-ai-studio\"  [!INCLUDE Studio]  ::: zone-end  ::: zone pivot=\"programming-language-python\"  [!INCLUDE Python]  ::: zone-end  ::: zone pivot=\"rest-api\"  [!INCLUDE REST]  ::: zone-end  [!INCLUDE Quota]",
